{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549874-someone-hacks-rite-of-the-fetish-egg-to-work-for-other-changing-breeds-what-now","id":1549874,"title":"Someone 'hacks' Rite of the Fetish Egg to work for other Changing Breeds. What now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-06T10:13:07-07:00","id":1549874,"title":"Someone 'hacks' Rite of the Fetish Egg to work for other Changing Breeds. What now?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>Rite of the Fetish Egg</b></u><br /> <br /> Level Two, Mystic<br /> <br /> The most important of all Corax rites, the Rite of the Fetish Egg births a new wereraven into the world. The binding requires a feather or hair from the \u201cparent\u201d with which to bind the spirit egg to the Corax-to-be. If anything happens to the egg or the binding before the First Change, the results are spiritually and psychologically devastating.<br /> <br /> System: This rite can only be performed in the Umbra, and requires a witness of the breed opposite that of the Corax \u201cparent.\u201d The Corax spends three hours and three permanent Gnosis creating the spirit egg, then another hour binding it to the soul for which it is intended. If the rite is interrupted at any point, the Gnosis is lost and the rite fails. </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that you can't use this Rite on a human who is the child of two Corax, but for most breeds that simply isn't possible as such a union would produce Metis.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine if some clever Theurging or some Bastet trickery, or a great heist pulled against Raven, or the intervention of some Incarna or somesuch, or maybe even some interference from a powerful Mage or Changeling, or an Ahadi inter-breed ritualist project, led to this Rite being 'cracked' to work for everyone.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the Garou, who place great importance upon heritage (some Tribes more than others of course!) would see this Gift as sacriligeous. Even if a typical Garou were to find out that a Corax is born and not made, that's Raven business, wolves are a breed apart.<br /> <br /> Here's how I see it playing out by Tribe and Breed, assuming there is nothing inherently wyrm-tainted or legitimately suspicious about the events.<br /> <br /> Black Furies: Opinions may be split; the ability to grant an exceptional girl or woman all of the Wyld's gifts, and bring her into the Tribe, would probably be highly valuable to some Furies. Others would naturally see it as an insult to Gaia and Luna.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: Would likely grab ahold of this with both hands. The ability for wise old Elders to turn 1-2 precocious humans (or wolves) into soldiers for the Tribe before dying would be seen as a huge boon.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: The main concern of the Children of Gaia would be to stop a war breaking out over the Rite's existence, either within the Nation or between Fera. It's easy to forget that the Children of Gaia are arguably the most war-ready of all the Tribes, with their take-all-comers recruitment, training of Kinfolk, and so on. Assuming that use of the Rite isn't more trouble than its worth, and doesn't tear the Nation apart, the Children would probably be making good use of it to bolster numbers in their own ranks in preparation for the coming wars of the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Fianna: I can't claim to be an expert on the Fianna, and I imagine that they would be split on this as you might expect a typical gathering of Garou to be. Those who value heritage and bloodlines will find it abhorrent, those who value deeds and potential might find it intriguing.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: Assuming the humans and wolves turned with the Rite are exceptional warriors, I could see the Get being very keen. Those who opposed it would likely do so with immediate and decisive violence, however, killing those who know the Rite and anyone near them. And maybe anyone who heard about it for good measure.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: Early adopters as always. I could see the Glass Walkers immediately converting some of their most militant Kinfolk into Ragabash, granting them the Gifts of the Garou without risking the Curse interfering with their work. The Glass Walkers would suffer, however, from being Homid-heavy and thus lacking the Gnosis-heavy Lupus who could create more Garou.<br /> <br /> Red Talons: Desperate times, desperate measures. The Red Talons would, hearing that the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers are creating Homids with this Rite, want in on the action to empower as many wolves as possible (hopefully making sure to leave enough wolves as 'regular' wolves to secure future breeding). They'd also be very quick to demand that the Tribes convert an equal number of wolves as they do humans; it's easy to forget that Red Talons are political animals and do engage in diplomacy!<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords: The play from the Shadow Lords would be focused on getting as much gain in power as possible. Their ideal position would be to corner the Silver Fangs into swearing to never, ever, EVER using the Rite, and then not backing them up in that commitment. They'd then plan to overwhelm the Silver Fangs with numbers and seek to supplant them as the leaders of the Garou Nation. That said, I do think it could play out very differently; if the Rite were received poorly by the Nation as a whole then they might seek to undermine and supplant any who tried supporting its use.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: The Striders have a lot of respect for the Corax, but beyond that I don't have a solid idea of what they'd do with this. If having enough Garou was the answer to defeat their enemies and reclaim their homeland... maybe?<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: Almost exclusively 100% against this Rite. Any suggestion of the other Tribes using this Rite would immediately place the Silver Fangs, who have a Pure Breed Entry Requirement, in a very difficult position. Both for political and religious reasons the Tribe could never, ever accept this Rite being used. So the question is basically &quot;what happens when every Tribe <i>except </i>for the Tribe who are &quot;&quot;&quot;in charge&quot;&quot;&quot; have reached a shared conclusion on a topic?&quot;<br /> <br /> Elder Brother: Given that the EB are extremely mystically inclined, I imagine their first interest would be how this was done, more than anything else. They might also be interested to see if there's any way Middle Brother Kinfolk could be turned into Garou with this Rite, as part of a project to restore the Tribe. I also wager that the Tribe would be very keen to recoup lost numbers and create more Garou among native peoples around the world.<br /> <br /> Younger Brother: Regenerating lost numbers and turning angry, disaffected and disempowered native Americans (and other indigenous peoples) into Garou would probably be quite high on their agenda. Fear that the other Tribes will use the Rite and then outnumber them would probably predominate. It would also be quite fitting, in their view I imagine, if they could ensure that every single Tribe of Native Americans across the US, Canada and so on had at least one Garou in its membership.<br /> <br /> Ajaba: Probably in favour of the Rite since it will help them regain numbers lost in the recent genocide.<br /> <br /> Ananasi: Given that the Ananasi aren't of 'Gaian' origin it's possible some would fear the Rite wouldn't work, but from what we can see the Ananasi are capable of joining 'packs' with Ovid in the Ahadi, and so presumably this Rite would work normally for Ananasi. I think the Ananasi would be keen to make use of this Rite if Queen Ananasa wanted them to use it, and if she forbade it, they would drop the idea entirely. QA would want to use the Rite if she thought it brought her closer to victory.<br /> <br /> Bastet: The mystically inclined would be curious to see if it worked, and the Bastet's pride would probably see some swearing they'll never stoop to artificially creating cubs, and others rushing to outdo the other Breeds.<br /> <br /> Gurahl: While the Gurahl would be very heavily incentivized to bolster their numbers, I imagine they would also be very fearful of the possible negative repercussions of massively swelling Shifter populations. There is a reason, after all, that they refused to share their life-restoring Rites with the Garou. The Gurahl might be very quick to encourage the other Shifters not to fall prey to the folly of massive recruitment drives, but this would probably be a losing battle.<br /> <br /> Kitsune: I have absolutely no idea what the Kitsune would make of this. I know they see themselves as being very pure of blood, so perhaps they'd balk at this much like the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> Mokole: Given that this probably has never happened before in all of the Mnesis records available to the various Streams, I'm sure the Mokole would be shocked more than anything. I also imagine they would want to remain impartial and watch carefully for what happens; Gaia made them to serve as her memory, not as her army or her fist, and so it makes sense that they would want to record and listen, and commit all events to memory in case warnings need to be carried into the far future against ever trying this again.<br /> <br /> Nagah: The Nagah rely on the sacred secret, and so mass recruitment doesn't suit them. Turning the most able young assassins in the world into weresnakes might be tempting however, in tiny numbers.<br /> <br /> Nuwisha: I imagine that the Nuwisha's views on this Rite would relate to whether they think it's wise. If they thought it wasn't then it would fall to them to prove it to the other Breeds in a teaching role.<br /> <br /> Ratkin: Given that the Rakin already have the Birthing Plague, I imagine they would only care about this with regards to the other Breeds multiplying, and with regards to whether the Rite was superior to the Birthing Plague. The Birthing Madness being circumvented might interest some Ratkin, but others might see that as sacriligeous.<br /> <br /> Rokea: Gaia's mission to the Rokea was to survive; being able to bring sharks into the fold could help with this. I think the Rokea would be slow to find out about this or react to it compared to the other Shifters.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to hear some ideas on what the various Tribes and Shifters would do in this scenario!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-06-2025, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T10:22:46-07:00","id":1549875,"title":"","content":"I think the Gurahl and Children of Gaia would also consider how to restore the Bunyip, Croatan, and the lost breeds (Apis, Camazotz, Grond).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T12:43:20-07:00","id":1549880,"title":"","content":"Just occurred to me that the requirement of an opposite-breed ally would present a big problem for the Red Talons. The Rite normally works with a Homid and Corvid Corax working together, with one as the main parent and the other as a witness, presumably dictated by Raven to keep the Corax in balance.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile for the Red Talons, and to a lesser extent the Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers, and some other Garou like Hakken, the Gift requiring an opposite-breed witness might be quite tricky. I can only see this being a massive problem for the Red Talons; other Garou may be low on Lupus, but they have them, and they have Lupus allies from other Tribes. The Red Talons do have Homid allies, but their tribal antipathy towards humans may make getting a Homid Garou to stand as witness quite difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T14:15:01-07:00","id":1549883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549874-someone-hacks-rite-of-the-fetish-egg-to-work-for-other-changing-breeds-what-now#post1549874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mokole: Given that this probably has never happened before in all of the Mnesis records available to the various Streams, I'm sure the Mokole would be shocked more than anything. I also imagine they would want to remain impartial and watch carefully for what happens; Gaia made them to serve as her memory, not as her army or her fist, and so it makes sense that they would want to record and listen, and commit all events to memory in case warnings need to be carried into the far future against ever trying this again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a minor nitpicking ^^<br /> There is a gift called <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Steal Shape </span></b><span style=\"color:black\">(Rank 5 </span></span></span></span>Midnight Sun (Shining) Gift, PGttCB 118-119, Mokole 85-86)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">It enables a Mokole to study the shape of another being for a span of time, and then take that shape as her new breed form.<br /> In this way, the Mokole have survived millennia of evolution on Gaia's Face. This Git is taught by a Lungfish spirit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><b>System:</b> The Mokole must study the new shape for at least a year. At the end of that time, she may spend a point of permanent Gnosis and assume the new shape.<br /> The shape must be close enough to the old one that her soul will inhabit it.<br /> The Storyteller is free to rule on what will and will not work.<br /> <u><i>Normally the Mokole will then pass this shape onto her offspring</i></u>, and they will replace one of her forms with the new.<br /> Only a few Mokole have ever managed to make this work, but is how a new varna comes to be able to incarnate shapeshifter souls, and is allegedly responsible for the rise of both the Corax and the Nagah. Some lore-masters say that all the Changing Breeds originated this way. However, this is unlikely.<br /> <br /> It is actually a very overlooked Gift and some book hint some outright state, yeah the Mokol\u00e9 tinkered with the early humans and &quot;responsible&quot; for the rise of Humanity and even adopted the Homid shape to survive to the modern era</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The jump from Dragons/Reptilians to Snakes (Nagah) and Birds (Croax) is basically easy, especially if you close the evolutionary gaps with a few generations and even mammals evolved from a common ancestor they shared with reptiles (the Kahara weird connection to the Mnesis was I thin kexplained with this ancestry, tho' I'm not sure)\u200b<br /> \u200b&quot;<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The shape must be close enough to the old one that her soul will inhabit it.</span></span></span>\u200b&quot; is very... broad requirement. And not really defined. But since the Mokol\u00e9 are anyweher between the tiny Gila monster (18 to 22.5 inches in length, a lizard), to the corcodiles and aligators and the Monitor Lizards (themselves are anything from an iguana, perenty and goanna to a Comodo Dragon) with the honorary mention to the Ao, the turtles and tortoises varna even &quot;in the Family&quot; they not even sometimes close to each other nor in look nor in size, or outright o na different branch of the evolutionary tree....<br /> And they do have a Homid but that could be explained with the Drachid &quot;Homo Reptilia&quot; Lizzid Peepl lost form...<br /> <br /> The Kucha Ekundu are a bloodline of the Red Talons who dwell in Africa and breed with African wild dogs (a.k.a. &quot;painted wolves&quot;) instead of true wolves. Some rumors claim that they learned this from the Mokol\u00e9.<br /> I don't really think it is a rumor... they basically jumped a whole genus<br /> The African wild dog (Lycaon pictus) is the member of the Lycaon Genus, Canidae Family in the Carnivor Order.<br /> The Wolf (Canis lupus) is the member of the Canis Genus, Canidae Family in the Carnivor Order.<br /> \u200b\u200bIt was quite a jump to move from on to the other to adapt and survive<br /> <br /> I think this hypotetical scenario you mentioned with the Croax Egg-Ritual is not that farfatched and actually happened just in another, a bit grander scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T19:30:16-07:00","id":1549890,"title":"","content":"The divide between wolves and African wild dogs is nothing compared to that between all the Canidae and the Tasmanian Wolf of the Bunyip. It's a freaking marsupial. Also, if the original breed of the Mokole was originally a dinosaur, then the Corax are probably more directly descended from the ancient Mokole than the modern Mokole.<br /> <br /> I think this exercise went a bit too far. Three Permanent Gnosis is a steep price, and the prep, time and risks impose yet more limitations. It <b>is</b> a game changer, but not a path to massive reproduction.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think every tribe would accept this rite soon or later, but the bigger change would come to tribes, breeds and Changing Breeds that suffer the most with low numbers. Among the Garou this rite would be the means for every tribe to increase their number of Lupus, and I actually think the Red Talons wouldn't face that a big of a problem finding willing witnesses. The dwindling number of Lupus Garou is everyone's problem, and this rite is an easy solution.<br /> <br /> Elder Brother wouldn't try to revive Middle Brother. Garou born true among Middle Brother's surviving kin is already a thing since always. What keeps the tribe from coming back is <b>not</b> a lack of kinfolk or of those kinfolk having Garou (those werewolves are initiated as members of either EB or YB tribes).<br /> <br /> Now, for the Changing Breeds, Ananasi, Ratkin and Rokea have little use for this rite. They don't have any problem with numbers, and actually compete for the spotlight as most numerous CBs, even more than the Garou. Nuwisha too, but with a twist: instead of large numbers, they have a predefined number in the material world. It is against their law to increase this number, when a new Nuwisha Changes, another Nuwisha leaves for the Umbra to never come back. It's weird as fuck, but it is what it is, so they wouldn't really have a big use for this rite.<br /> <br /> Guhral, Kitsune and <i>some</i> Bastet would be far more likely to benefit from this rite. Even then, few Bastet would care enough to give up so much. The Guhral are keenly aware of the dangers of overpopulation, but they currently suffer from <i><b>under</b></i>population. They're likely to make judicious use of the rite, even given the steep price.<br /> <br /> When it comes to reproduction, being a Kitsune <i><b>sucks</b></i>. It sucks so much that most of them will probably think that losing 3 Gnosis on an adoptive child beats having a new Kitsune through normal means (and killing one or both of the parents). The next step would be to find a Fetish condom or a Vasectomy rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T02:28:48-07:00","id":1549901,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> it's worth keeping in mind that Garou execute their criminals and most Tribes do practice mandatory euthanasia (i.e. execution of the sick, old and disabled). There's a lot of permanent Gnosis out there ready to be spent, even if it's reasonably hard to come by like you say.<br /> <br /> For example, I think given a choice between &quot;create a new Lupus Garou, then suffer a Punishment Rite and redeem yourself, or be executed now for your crime&quot; many Garou would choose to live, even if some would choose to die. And a Garou who is about to undergo the Rite of the Winter Wolf would probably leap at the chance to create another soldier for Gaia before they go. There will probably also be Garou in Harano who would volunteer to create new Garou and would need to be discouraged from burning their permanent Gnosis, as in &quot;you're going to get better, don't give up on yourself and burn all your power to make a new cub&quot;.<br /> <br /> Good points about the problems with Middle Brother, and the underpopulation of the Gurahl etc.<br /> <br /> I'd still argue that the Ratkin would be interested in the Rite if it allowed a way to create Ratkin who lack the Birthing Madness. If that sidestep worked they might view it as a useful way to add non-insane Ratkin to their ranks, or ban it as sacrilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-07-2025, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T02:43:43-07:00","id":1549903,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> keep in mind that this Rite only works on a fitting recipient, a human or a raven (or, in the case of Garou, a wolf etc.)<br /> <br /> So it isn't a giant gamechanger in terms of species. A Garou who was ready to risk losing 3 permanent Gnosis for nothing could try and do the rite on a dog and see what happens, but I'd call that extremely unwise, for example. There isn't really anything about the Rite which lets you pull off stuff like &quot;wereshibes!&quot;, it lets you make more regular Garou, which is possibly a gamechanger, but it would be impacting numbers of existing Breeds, rather than messing around with weirder stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T13:52:50-07:00","id":1549956,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I think that Kitsune would adopt the rite so readily that soon all Kitsune would be born using it. With the Kitsune's elitist tendencies, they would also welcome the chance to select the most promising candidates to be turned into Kitsune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}